#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157072 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15241dd-898f-5f1c-9c1c-469a4af1fb80" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Inequality Involving an Exponential Function and a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "21071a31-a79e-5aa4-9a57-8ce642770adb" :question/math-academy-id "e-7663" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\dfrac{(x^2-8)^3}{11^x} \\geq 0$." :question/worked-solution "When we have an inequality involving an exponential function with a positive base, we're allowed to multiply or divide both sides by the exponential function.\n\nMultiplying both sides of the given inequality by $11^x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}((x^{2} - 8)^{3})/(11^{x}) & \\ge 0 \\\\ 11^{x} \\cdot ((x^{2} - 8)^{3})/(11^{x}) & \\ge 11^{x} \\cdot 0 \\\\ (x^{2} - 8)^{3} & \\ge 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{(x^{2} - 8)^{3}}\\begin{vmatrix}\\ge \\sqrt[3]{0} \\\\ x^{2} - 8\\end{vmatrix}\\ge 0; x^{2}\\begin{vmatrix}\\ge 8 \\\\ \\sqrt{x^{2}}\\end{vmatrix}\\ge \\sqrt{8}; \\mid x \\mid \\mid \\ge 2\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -2\\sqrt 2\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2 \\sqrt 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157073 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "479e5736-efe1-5e94-929f-3dcd6d13a733" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with the Same Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "9e1ccbcf-23bb-5df5-aa02-cb90a9421396" :question/math-academy-id "e-7664" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x^2e^{x+1}-2e^{x+1} < -xe^{x+1}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{2}e^{x + 1} - 2e^{x + 1} & < - xe^{x + 1} \\\\ x^{2}e^{x + 1} + xe^{x + 1} - 2e^{x + 1} & < 0 \\\\ (x^{2} + x - 2)e^{x + 1} & < 0 \\\\ (x + 2)(x - 1)e^{x + 1} & < 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $e^{x+1}$ and get\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-1) < 0\n$$\n\nThis represents an upwards parabola whose roots are at $x=-2$ and $x=1$. The parabola is below the $x$-axis when $-2 < x < 1$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2859/Source/Images/9bc30ffe9a0c96ace6cb684a3dbd1068.png)\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2 < x < 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "35c42ff1-2381-5fb4-b04b-cbe790e1d667" :question/math-academy-id "e-7665" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $x^5 \\cdot 4^{x} > 4^{x - 15}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we move all the terms to the left side of the inequality and factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{5} \\cdot 4^{x} & > 4^{x - 15} \\\\ x^{5} \\cdot 4^{x} - 4^{x - 15} & > 0 \\\\ (x^{5} - 4^{-15}) \\cdot 4^{x} & > 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we divide both sides by $4^{x}$ and get\n\n$$\nx^5 - 4^{-15} > 0\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x^{5} & > 4^{-15} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{x^{5}} & > \\sqrt[5]{4^{-15}} \\\\ x & > (4^{-15})^{1/5} \\\\ x & > 4^{-3} \\\\ x & > \\frac{1}{64}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx > \\dfrac{1}{64}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving Exponential Functions with Different Exponents and a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b282b7-3d62-5fbd-a721-e0e94c2a7181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le 0$ or $x \\ge 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156359} {:answer/id #uuid "0b53fec1-b30d-5d9f-a33c-665834a70977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0 \\le x \\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156360} {:answer/id #uuid "443d4ceb-d027-5ca0-8b57-a260f5bce1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156361} {:answer/id #uuid "548ece35-3b60-5221-997a-80ec664e36ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "all real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156362} {:answer/id #uuid "75c3926e-c51b-5d8c-8bdc-a57f69f13af3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le - 3$ or $x \\ge 0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b282b7-3d62-5fbd-a721-e0e94c2a7181" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le 0$ or $x \\ge 3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156359} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a20aa5-2832-5d35-8d27-37e2cdef5624" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156358}] :question/id #uuid "485dd702-22ef-5672-ba6d-aa433fac1c74" :question/math-academy-id "q-87772" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3^{4x}x^{2} \\ge 3^{4x + 1}x$."}]}
